# check-tick-launches.allow -- calls scripts/check-tick-launches.sh does not
# follow, each with the reason the callee's launch is never reached that way.
#
# One record per line: <caller><TAB><callee><TAB><reason>, both paths from the
# plugin root. A record exempts that one call, not the callee: a template or
# another script that runs the callee is still followed into it. A record that
# no longer matches a call the templates reach fails the check, so it is
# removed with the call it described.
skills/coordinate/scripts/reconcile-legs.sh	skills/coordinate/scripts/dispatch-worker.sh	reconcile-legs.sh runs it only as --releg-imported, which exits before the niwa dispatch of the dispatch path
skills/work-on/scripts/verification-route.sh	scripts/check-skill.sh	verification-route.sh only names it, as a path whose change closes the hosted-of-record route and as a file it reads at the merge-base with git show; it never runs it
skills/work-on/scripts/verification-route.sh	scripts/skill-gate.sh	verification-route.sh only names it, as a path whose change closes the hosted-of-record route and as a file it reads at the merge-base with git show; it never runs it
skills/work-on/scripts/verification-route.sh	skills/work-on/scripts/verification-hosted-coverage_test.sh	verification-route.sh only names it, as a path whose change closes the hosted-of-record route; it never runs it
